      <section style="background: #161022; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 8px; padding: 24px; margin-bottom: 36px;">
        <h2 id="power-curve-trajectory-early-vs-mid-vs-end-game" style="font-size: 1.3rem; color: #fff; margin: 0 0 16px;">Power Curve Trajectory: Early vs Mid vs End Game</h2>
        <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 14px;">
          <div style="background: #0d0a14; padding: 14px 16px; border-radius: 6px; border-left: 3px solid #eab308;">
            <strong style="color: #eab308;">Early Game (Levels 1–10): Balanced Progression</strong>
            <p style="color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.5; margin: 4px 0 0;">
              Starting with 90 HP and 8 ATK / 12 MAG, the Bard progresses smoothly through Act 1. Basic sonic strikes deal consistent damage, while early anthem buffs provide reliable combat buffers.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div style="background: #0d0a14; padding: 14px 16px; border-radius: 6px; border-left: 3px solid #34d399;">
            <strong style="color: #34d399;">Mid Game (Levels 11–20): High Group Utility</strong>
            <p style="color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.5; margin: 4px 0 0;">
              Unlocking Minstrel, Siren, or Pianist at Level 15 transforms the Bard into an indispensable asset for group dungeon runs. Rondo of Alacrity allows your team to skip monster turns in Act 2.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div style="background: #0d0a14; padding: 14px 16px; border-radius: 6px; border-left: 3px solid #f43f5e;">
            <strong style="color: #f43f5e;">End Game (Levels 21–30): S+ Tier Raid Essential</strong>
            <p style="color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.5; margin: 4px 0 0;">
              In Torment Mode and Abyss Raids, having a Minstrel or Pianist is non-negotiable. Action gauge manipulation and +25% party damage buffs are the only reliable way to break high-tier raid boss enrage timers.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Best-in-Slot Equipment Synergies -->
      <section style="background: #161022; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 8px; padding: 24px; margin-bottom: 36px;">
        <h2 id="recommended-best-in-slot-equipment-synergies" style="font-size: 1.3rem; color: #c9a227; margin: 0 0 16px;">Recommended Best-in-Slot Equipment Synergies</h2>
        <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 14px;">
          <div style="background: #0d0a14; padding: 14px 16px; border-radius: 6px;">
            <strong style="color: #eab308;">Weapon: Golden Harp of the Virtuoso or Flute of Harmony</strong>
            <p style="color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.5; margin: 4px 0 0;">
              Grants +28 ATK, +36 MAG, and extends the active duration of all anthem songs by 1 additional turn.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div style="background: #0d0a14; padding: 14px 16px; border-radius: 6px;">
            <strong style="color: #38bdf8;">Armor Set: Troubadour Feathered Tunic (Tier 3 Set)</strong>
            <p style="color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.5; margin: 4px 0 0;">
              Provides +38 DEF, +16 SPD, and +15% Party Anthem Radius. Ensures your songs reach allies across large arena chambers.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div style="background: #0d0a14; padding: 14px 16px; border-radius: 6px;">
            <strong style="color: #c9a227;">Accessory: Metronome of the Maestro</strong>
            <p style="color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.5; margin: 4px 0 0;">
              Restores 1 Energy Point to all party members whenever an Ultimate Anthem song is successfully resolved.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Frequently Asked Questions -->
      <section style="background: #161022; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 8px; padding: 24px; margin-bottom: 36px;">
        <h2 id="frequently-asked-questions-about-the-bard" style="font-size: 1.3rem; color: #fff; margin: 0 0 16px;">Frequently Asked Questions About the Bard</h2>
        <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 16px;">
          <div>
            <h3 id="do-bard-anthems-stack-with-warrior-and-mage-buffs" style="font-size: 1.05rem; color: #c9a227; margin: 0 0 6px;">Do Bard anthems stack with warrior and mage buffs?</h3>
            <p style="color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.9rem; line-height: 1.5; margin: 0;">
              Yes. Bard anthem buffs occupy a unique "Musical Aura" slot that stacks multiplicatively with warrior battle shouts, food buffs, and mage spell enchantments.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 id="can-bard-songs-be-interrupted-if-damaged" style="font-size: 1.05rem; color: #c9a227; margin: 0 0 6px;">Can Bard songs be interrupted if damaged?</h3>
            <p style="color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.9rem; line-height: 1.5; margin: 0;">
              Anthem songs that cast instantly resolve immediately on your turn. However, channeling songs like Battle Symphony can be interrupted if the Bard is afflicted with Stun or Silence. Equipping Seraph or Dullahan prevents this hazard.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 id="which-super-class-is-best-for-guild-raids-minstrel-or-pianist" style="font-size: 1.05rem; color: #c9a227; margin: 0 0 6px;">Which Super Class is best for Guild Raids: Minstrel or Pianist?</h3>
            <p style="color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.9rem; line-height: 1.5; margin: 0;">
              Minstrel is preferred for speed-running and burst damage teams. Pianist is superior for progression raids where prolonged energy sustainability and team healing are required to survive enrage phases.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

